# The Rat King falls — and something comes back up the stairs.
@id crown_of_spoons
@title The Crown of Spoons
@trigger boss_beaten 3
@order 50

== start
pip (happy): WE WON! The Rat King is having a very long nap!
pip (neutral): And — look what he was sitting on. Right at the top of the spoon pile.
narrator: A dented copper ladle. Two letters scratched into the handle: M & R.
maro (surprised): …
? flag maro_opened -> knows
maro (sad): That's Rook's. My old partner. He dropped it covering me. I thought it was gone for good.
-> choice

== knows
maro (sad): Rook's ladle. Twenty years on a rat's throne.
pip (sad): He stood his ground. Like you said.
maro (happy): …Yes. Yes, he did.

== choice
maro (neutral): Hm. Tonight I cook the Feast. My way.
* "Hang it over the pass. Rook cooks with us now."
  ~ bonus cook_speed +0.10
  ~ flag ladle_pass
  maro (happy): Over the pass. He'd like that. Nosy man — always watching the plates.
* "It's yours, Maro. Keep it close."
  ~ affinity maro +2
  ~ bonus price +0.05
  maro (sad): …Thank you.
  maro (happy): Every dish I cook with it gets a little extra care. They'll taste it.
* "What if Rook made it out?"
  ~ flag find_rook
  ~ affinity pip +1
  pip (surprised): Wait — they never found him, right? So he could be ANYWHERE!
  maro (neutral): Twenty years, Pip.
  pip (happy): I've got a compass that points at lost people. I'm just saying.
narrator: That night the Feast goes out to every stool, and Maro hums the whole time.
-> end
